Why don't you play in Wizard mode if you want to cheat?

If it hasn't been disabled while compiling (it hasn't in the official
executables, e.g. nh313386.exe for the MS-DOS/386-version), Wizard
a.k.a. debug mode can be started with one of the following commands:
nethack -u wizard -D
nethack -uwizard -D

When in a Wizard-mode game, press ? and look at the Wizard mode command
list...

>I'd love to change a wand's charges from say, 7, to 99.  I just don't know
>where in the savefile I would look for those stats...

In Wizard mode it's easy. Just press ^W and wish for e.g. a blessed wand
of death (100). Or anything else that you want (yes, even the Amulet of
Yendor!).

